module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.unsafe_candidate_swapped_into_a_running_service

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data unsafe_candidate_swapped_into_a_running_service: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "unsafe_candidate_swapped_into_a_running_service" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a live-deploy apply switches the running service onto a candidate that was not admitted for that target — either the serve entry does not compile, or the checkout is not the branch that target may install. HARM: the running revision is replaced by a crash-loop (lab, source annotation inside a fn body, learned only at readiness) or by a development checkout aimed at production (gunbc converge --host srv1 --mode deploy on a dev branch, stopped by hand).",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: readiness and a human stop are AFTER the mutation. The 2026-10-09 empty --candidate-branch admit (fleet_converge_deploy_branch_admits) is the hole that let a nonempty non-main checkout through to production. The serve-entry hole is the missing compile of the declared serve entry before the unit swap.",

    "REPAIR: gunbc.live_deploy.pre_swap_admission live_deploy_pre_swap_admission, one decision. Each DesiredDeployment row carries admitted_branch as NonEmptyStr (production main; lab its integration branch, read from the instance through dispatch_base_branch, gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dashboard_instance srv1_lab_publication_base_branch; srv2 declares main) (gunbc.design_ruling production_is_main_only_lab_admits_integration). The serve-entry compile is the candidate's own compiler over the serve route: observe_serve_entry_compile_clean runs the checkout's gunbc (gunbc.WitnessBin.Run) as compile --entry DeploymentServiceConfig.serve_entry --target dag under gunbc.live_deploy.spec deployment_serve_source_roots, the roots the emitted ExecStart passes to serve, and serve_entry_compile_verdict_of reads its exit and error lines (exit 0 admits; a nonzero exit with error lines is blocked and carries them; a nonzero exit without them is unobserved). A blocking or unobserved compile refuses. The compile_dag_diagnostic_census builtin is not consulted: its declared scope is a synthetic single-module source on the Rust target and it refused real candidates whose serve entry compiles clean. A detached HEAD is admitted for branch B only when git.Inspect.MergeBase of HEAD and refs/remotes/origin/<B> equals HEAD (checkout_branch_for_admission); GITHUB_REF_NAME is not read. Both CI (live_deploy_admitted_wet_with_access, live_deploy_transaction_admitted) and operator-local (live_deploy_operator_local_admitted, fleet_converge_operator_cli_dispatch) consult it after the candidate is named and before access preflight or receipted apply. A refusal states that nothing was mutated.",

    "CLAIMS: test.claim.live_deploy.pre_swap_admission_witness a_non_main_revision_aimed_at_production_refuses, a_detached_candidate_not_reachable_from_main_is_refused_for_production, a_blocking_compile_refuses_with_nothing_mutated, a_blocking_compile_refusal_names_what_blocked_it, a_nonzero_exit_without_an_error_line_is_unobserved_not_clean; controls main_aimed_at_production_admits, a_detached_candidate_reachable_from_main_is_admitted, a_named_branch_checkout_ignores_merge_base_standing, operator_local_admission_does_not_consult_github_ref_name, lab_dev_aimed_at_lab_admits, a_clean_compile_on_main_to_production_proceeds, a_zero_exit_is_admitted_whatever_it_printed. Inhabitance: test.claim.live_deploy.pre_swap_admission_merge_base_inhabitance_witness git_merge_base_in_a_temp_repo_emits_the_standing_admission_consumes; test.claim.live_deploy.pre_swap_admission_serve_compile_inhabitance_witness the_checkouts_serve_entry_compiles_clean_through_the_gate_route, a_staged_type_error_entry_is_blocked_by_real_execution, a_staged_clean_entry_is_admitted_by_real_execution.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable — the failure occurred on the host (crash-loop; a hand-stopped production aim). RUNG NOW: 1, mitigatable — the decision fold refuses on supplied standings, including a detached HEAD whose merge-base is not HEAD while a CI event name would have said main, and a wet inhabitance claim runs git merge-base over a temp repo; those claims are not on the required witnesses path (v2-bootstrap), so DESIGN §4b does not establish rung 2. A prior row that said rung 2 while naming that gap was rung inflation (review 80259). CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed — target class, detached ancestry, and compile standing are decidable from the selected identity, git ancestry, and a compile of the declared serve entry. NEXT TRIGGER: those admission claims (and a wet apply of a fixture-broken serve entry or of a non-main detached checkout at production that leaves the host tree and unit unchanged) execute on the required witnesses path.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
